    "body": "### What does this PR do?\n\nThe quantized (fp8) branch of the async weight sync feeds every bucket straight into `load_quanted_weights`. For a model with `tie_word_embeddings=True` the trainer state dict carries both `model.embed_tokens.weight` and its alias `lm_head.weight`, and the two can land in different buckets. vLLM 0.29 checks skipped aliases per `load_weights` call, so a bucket that carries only the alias fails the check and the first sync aborts:\n\n```\nValueError: 'lm_head.weight' was skipped because it is tied to 'model.embed_tokens.weight' in Qwen3ForCausalLM, but 'model.embed_tokens.weight' was not found in the checkpoint, so the tied weight is uninitialized.\n```\n\nThe standard (non-quantized) branch already filters the alias through `drop_tied_alias_updates` (#7973); the fp8 branch was left out. This PR applies the same filter there, including the MTP drafter call, and adds a CPU regression test.\n\nReproduced with Qwen3-0.6B, `actor_rollout_ref.rollout.quantization=fp8`, vLLM 0.29.0: the first weight sync failed before the fix and a 3-step GRPO run completed after it.\n\n### Checklist Before Starting\n\n- [x] Search for similar PRs: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+tied+embedding+fp8 and https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+drop_tied_alias_updates (only #7973, which covers the standard branch)\n- [x] Format the PR title as `[{modules}] {type}: {description}`\n\n### Test\n\n```\npython -m pytest tests/utils/test_vllm_weight_name_normalization_on_cpu.py -q\n# 28 passed (vLLM 0.29.0); the new test fails on main and passes with the fix\n```\n\n### Design & Code Changes\n\n- `verl/workers/rollout/vllm_rollout/utils.py`: pass `param_updates` through `drop_tied_alias_updates` before `load_quanted_weights` (main model and drafter).\n- `tests/utils/test_vllm_weight_name_normalization_on_cpu.py`: `test_quantized_sync_drops_tied_alias_updates`.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used; every changed line was reviewed and the tests above were run by the submitter.\n\n### Checklist Before Submitting\n\n- [x] Read the [Contribute Guide](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] Apply [pre-commit checks](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#code-linting-and-formatting).\n- [x] Add / Update the documentation: not needed.\n- [x] Add unit or end-to-end test(s): CPU test above, collected by the existing CPU unit-test workflow.\n- [ ] Once your PR is ready for CI, send a message in the `ci-request` channel.\n",
